  "summary": "Sudanese writer Tayeb Salih's novel Mawsim al-hijra ila al-shamal appeared in Arabic in 1966, first in a Beirut magazine and then as a book. It follows two Sudanese men who studied in England. In Banipal magazine's 2018 poll of 100 best Arabic novels it came first, with 61 nominations.",
